    "content": "FORMAT B-19  -  UNDERTAKING / COMPLIANCE WITH NOTICE OF\nAPPEARANCE UNDER SECTION 35(3) BNSS\nPre-Trial / Complaint & FIR\nTO,\nTHE STATION HOUSE OFFICER / INVESTIGATING OFFICER,\nPOLICE STATION .............................................., DISTT. ..............................\nSUBJECT: COMPLIANCE WITH THE NOTICE OF APPEARANCE DATED .......................... ISSUED\nUNDER SECTION 35(3) OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023 IN FIR NO.\n.......................... OF 20........., POLICE STATION ..............................\nUNDERTAKING AND COMPLIANCE WITH THE NOTICE OF APPEARANCE ISSUED\nUNDER SECTION 35(3) OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023\nMOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:\n1. That the undersigned has received the Notice of Appearance bearing No. .......................... dated\n.......................... issued by you under Section 35(3) of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023,\ndirecting the undersigned to appear before you on .......................... at ............ hours in connection with the\nabove-mentioned FIR.\n2. That the undersigned hereby acknowledges the receipt of the said notice, and states that the undersigned has\nnot, at any point of time, refused to cooperate with the investigation and has no intention of evading the\nprocess of law.\n3. That in compliance with the said notice, the undersigned appeared before you on .......................... at ............\nhours and joined the investigation, and submitted all such documents and information as were required: (i)\n..............................; (ii) ..............................; (iii) ..............................\n4. That the undersigned undertakes as under:\n(a) That the undersigned shall appear before you or before such officer or Court as may be required, on every\ndate and at every place as may be intimated to me, without fail;\n(b) That the undersigned shall render all cooperation in the investigation and shall produce all documents and\narticles in my possession or control, which are relevant to the investigation, as and when called upon to do so;\n(c) That the undersigned shall not, directly or indirectly, make any inducement, threat or promise to any person\nacquainted with the facts of the case, so as to dissuade such person from disclosing such facts to the Court or to\nthe police;\n(d) That the undersigned shall not tamper with the evidence, and shall not influence any witness in any manner\nwhatsoever;\n(e) That the undersigned shall not leave India without the prior permission of the competent authority/Court;\n(f) That the undersigned shall keep you informed of my current address and mobile number, and shall inform\nyou of any change therein forthwith.\n5. That by virtue of the provisions of Section 35(5), BNSS, 2023, since the undersigned has complied with the\nterms of the notice and continues to do so, the undersigned shall not be arrested in connection with the\nabove-noted FIR, unless you record reasons in writing for doing so and such reasons are justified in the\nfacts and circumstances of the case.\n6. That the undersigned requests that a receipt/acknowledgement of this undertaking and compliance be given\nto the undersigned, and that the same be placed on the record of the investigation.\nPRAYER:\n\nIt is, therefore, most respectfully prayed that you may kindly be pleased to:\n(i) take on record this undertaking and the compliance of the notice issued under Section 35(3), BNSS, 2023;\n(ii) permit the undersigned to join the investigation and to produce the necessary documents in support of\nhis/her defence, and to remain present through the counsel as and when permissible;\n(iii) not arrest the undersigned in view of the compliance with the notice, in terms of Section 35(5), BNSS,\n2023; and\n(iv) grant a receipt/acknowledgement of this compliance and apprise the undersigned of the further course of\nthe investigation.\nAPPLICANT / NOTICE-EE\nTHROUGH\nADVOCATE\nPlace: ..............................\nDate: ..............................\nNOTES, PRACTICE POINTS AND DOCUMENTS TO BE ANNEXED\n[Note: (i) Compliance with the notice under Section 35(3) is the sine qua non for the protection granted by Section 35(5),\nBNSS, 2023. Therefore, the notice must never be ignored, and the date and time of appearance must be strictly obeyed. (ii) If\nthe date mentioned in the notice is inconvenient, a written request for an alternative date should be made in advance, in\nwriting, with reasons; this will obviate the charge of non-compliance. (iii) The acknowledgement/receipt of the appearance and\nof the documents submitted must always be obtained and preserved - this is the applicant's principal defence against a\nsubsequent allegation of non-cooperation. (iv) If, despite compliance, the police attempt to arrest the applicant, an application\nunder Section 482, BNSS, 2023 (anticipatory bail) may be moved immediately, or the arrest may be challenged as being\ncontrary to Section 35, BNSS, 2023.]\nCR.P.C. EQUIVALENT\nOld Section 41A, Cr.P.C., 1973 -> Section 35(3) to (6), BNSS, 2023. Old Section 41B -> Section 36, BNSS, 2023.\nPRECEDENTS REFERRED TO\n• Arnesh Kumar v. State of Bihar, (2014) 8 SCC 273 - the notice of appearance must be issued where arrest is not required;\nfailure to comply with the notice justifies arrest.\n• Satender Kumar Antil v. CBI, (2022) 10 SCC 51 - for offences punishable with imprisonment up to seven years, the notice of\nappearance is the norm and arrest is the exception, unless the statutory conditions for arrest are satisfied."
