    "category": "crime",
    "categoryLabel": "Crime",
    "statute": "Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 (Section 348)",
    "title": "Application for Recall / Re-Examination of Witness & Summoning Material Witness (Section 348 BNSS)",
    "shortDesc": "Comprehensive petition under Section 348 BNSS (old Section 311 CrPC) to summon any material witness or recall and re-examine witness essential to just decision.",
    "limitationNotice": "Wide Powers: Can be exercised at any stage before judgment; no limitation of stage or number of applications.",
    "tags": [
      "Recall Witness",
      "Section 348 BNSS",
      "311 CrPC",
      "Material Witness",
      "Crime"
    ],
    "content": "FORMAT E-44  -  APPLICATION FOR RECALL / RE-EXAMINATION OF A\nWITNESS AND FOR SUMMONING MATERIAL WITNESS\nTrial Stage\nIN THE COURT OF .............................., (DISTRICT ..............................)\nCRIMINAL CASE NO. .......................... OF 20.........\nIN THE MATTER OF:\n...................................................................., S/o .............................., R/o .............................................. ...........\nAPPLICANT / ACCUSED\nTHE STATE .............................................. ........... RESPONDENT\nFIR NO. .......................... OF 20........., POLICE STATION ..............................\nAPPLICATION FOR RECALL OF WITNESS / SUMMONING OF MATERIAL WITNESS\nUNDER SECTION 348 OF THE BHARATIYA NAGARIK SURAKSHA SANHITA, 2023\nMOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:\n1. That the applicant/accused is facing trial in the above-noted case for offences punishable under Sections\n.............................. of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, and the trial is at the stage of the evidence of the\nprosecution/defence.\n2. That Section 348, BNSS, 2023 (old Section 311, Cr.P.C.) provides that any Court may, at any stage of any\ninquiry, trial or other proceeding under the Sanhita, summon any person as a witness, or examine any\nperson in attendance, though not summoned as a witness, or recall and re-examine any person already\nexamined; and the Court shall summon and examine or recall and re-examine any such person if his\nevidence appears to it to be essential to the just decision of the case.\n3. That the following witness(es), namely .............................. (name and particulars), is/are material and\nessential for the just decision of the case, in that the said witness(es) .............................. (set out the\nspecific relevance of the evidence - e.g., is an eye-witness to the occurrence; is the author of the document\nrelied upon by the prosecution; is the person who prepared the forensic report; is the owner of the vehicle\ninvolved in the accident; is the doctor who conducted the post-mortem/medical examination; is the\ncustodian of the electronic record).\nOR\n4. That the witness .............................., who was examined before this Hon'ble Court on .........................., is\nrequired to be recalled and re-examined, in that the following material aspects could not be put to the said\nwitness on account of .............................. (state the reason - e.g., the document .............................. was\nproduced/proved after the examination of the witness; the certified copy of .............................. was\nobtained on ..........................; the evidence of the subsequent witness .............................. has rendered the\nre-examination of the said witness necessary; the witness has, in his evidence, referred to a document,\nnamely .............................., which was not available at the time of his examination), and the recall of the\nsaid witness is essential for the just decision of the case.\n5. That the evidence sought to be elicited from the witness is directly relevant to the issues involved in the case\nand would assist this Hon'ble Court in arriving at the truth. The application is not being made with the\nobject of delaying the trial or of filling up the lacunae in the defence, but is bona fide and necessary.\n6. That the power under Section 348, BNSS, 2023 is a salutary power conferred upon the Court with the object\nof discovering the truth and doing justice, and it is well settled that the said power is not fettered by any\nlimitation as to the stage at which it may be exercised; the only precondition is that the evidence must\nappear to the Court to be essential to the just decision of the case.\n\n7. That the Hon'ble Supreme Court has held that the power under Section 311, Cr.P.C. (now Section 348,\nBNSS, 2023) is to be exercised liberally and that if the evidence is essential for the just decision of the\ncase, the Court must summon and examine the witness, notwithstanding that the application is made at a\nbelated stage; the Court must, however, not exercise the power to cause prejudice to the accused or to fill\nup the lacunae in the prosecution case.\n8. That the applicant undertakes to bear the costs of the summoning and examination of the said witness, and to\nabide by such conditions as this Hon'ble Court may impose, including the condition of payment of the\ncosts to the witness/complainant.\nPRAYER:\nIt is, therefore, most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may kindly be pleased to:\n(i) summon .............................................., S/o .............................., R/o .............................................., as a\nwitness in the above-noted case, and permit the examination of the said witness/direction for the\nproduction of the documents, namely .............................., in terms of Section 348 of the Bharatiya\nNagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023;\n(ii) in the alternative, recall and re-examine the witness .............................................., who was examined\nbefore this Hon'ble Court on .........................., for the purposes of putting the questions and the\ndocuments which could not be put at the time of the original examination, the evidence of the said\nwitness being essential for the just decision of the case;\n(iii) issue the appropriate summons/process to the said witness and direct the prosecution/defence, as the case\nmay be, to produce the necessary documents; and\n(iv) pass such other and further order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper.\nAPPLICANT / ACCUSED\nTHROUGH\nADVOCATE\nPlace: ..............................\nDate: ..............................\nNOTES, PRACTICE POINTS AND DOCUMENTS TO BE ANNEXED\n[Note: (i) The discretion under Section 348, BNSS, 2023 is very wide and is to be exercised to discover the truth. The Court may\nact on its own motion as well. (ii) The application should be specific as to the name of the witness, the purpose of the\nexamination and the relevance of the evidence. (iii) Where the application is made at the instance of the accused, the Court\nshould ordinarily grant it if the evidence is essential, subject to costs. (iv) The Court must record reasons for allowing or\nrejecting the application. (v) The power cannot be exercised to fill up the lacunae in the prosecution case or to cause prejudice\nto the accused. (vi) An order rejecting a bona fide application under Section 348 is a curable irregularity only if no prejudice is\ncaused; otherwise, it may vitiate the trial.]\nCR.P.C. EQUIVALENT\nOld Section 311, Cr.P.C., 1973 -> Section 348, BNSS, 2023.\nPRECEDENTS REFERRED TO\n• Mohanlal Shamji Soni v. Union of India, 1991 Supp (1) SCC 271 - the scope of Section 311, Cr.P.C.; the power must be\nexercised liberally to discover the truth.\n• Rajendra Prasad v. Narcotic Cell, (1999) 6 SCC 110 - the power under Section 311 is not to be exercised to fill up the lacunae\nin the prosecution case or to cause prejudice to the accused.\n• U.T. of Dadra & Nagar Haveli v. Fatehsinh Mohansinh Chauhan, (2006) 7 SCC 529 - the power under Section 311 is\ndiscretionary and is to be exercised in the interests of justice.\n• Iddar v. Aabida, (2007) 11 SCC 215 - the recall of a witness for cross-examination; the test of necessity.\n• Varsha Garg v. State of M.P., (2022) SCC OnLine SC 986 - the Court's power to summon a witness; the principles to be\napplied."
