    "content": "NDPS Act, 1985  -  Drafting, Pleadings, Forms & Formats\nB-1. Vakalatnama and Memorandum of Appearance\nPurpose\nThe first document filed in every NDPS case on the defence side: the instrument by which the advocate is\nengaged, followed by the memorandum of appearance and, where the accused is in custody or exempted, the\napplication for exemption from personal appearance.\nStatutory basis\nSection 303 CrPC / section 340 BNSS (right of the accused to be defended by a pleader of his choice); Advocates\nAct, 1961; Bar Council of India Rules. In Delhi practice the Vakalatnama is filed with the memorandum of\nappearance and an affidavit of the pairokar identifying the accused.\nModel Vakalatnama\nIN THE COURT OF THE LEARNED SPECIAL JUDGE (NDPS), [DISTRICT COURTS / SAKET COURTS], [CITY]\n \nSC No. __ of 20____________________\nFIR No. __ of 20____________________\nPolice Station : ____________________\nUnder Sections : 20 / 21 / 22 / 25 / 27-A / 29 of the NDPS Act, 1985\n \nIN THE MATTER OF:\n \nSTATE (Through PS ____________________)                                   .... PROSECUTION\nVERSUS\n[NAME OF ACCUSED] S/o [Father's name], R/o [Address]               .... ACCUSED\n \nVAKALATNAMA\n \nI, [Name of accused], son/daughter of [name], resident of [address], the accused in the above case, do hereby appoint and \nretain [Name of Advocate], Advocate, [chamber address], telephone __, e-mail __, to appear, act and plead for me before \nthis Hon'ble Court and/or before any other court, tribunal or authority in the above case, and to file applications, \naffidavits, documents, to receive notices, to withdraw or compromise the case, to deposit, receive and refund amounts, \nand generally to do all acts necessary for the conduct of the case, on my behalf and at my risk.\n \nI undertake to ratify and confirm all acts done by my Advocate in the conduct of this case.\n \nDated: __                                             ____________________\nPlace: __                                              (Signature / L.T.I. of the Accused)\n \nACCEPTANCE\n \nAccepted.\nDated: __                                             ____________________\nPlace: __                                              (Signature of the Advocate)\n \nIdentified by:\n[Name of identifier], [relation], R/o [address]                  ____________________\nDrafting notes\n•  Two copies. File the original in the court record and retain an acknowledged copy. Where the accused is in\njudicial custody, the Vakalatnama is ordinarily got executed in jail and attested by the jail authorities; the\nattested copy must be filed along with the affidavit of the pairokar.\n•  Pairokar. In Delhi and several other States, the practice is to file an affidavit of a pairokar (relative or friend\nof the accused) verifying the contents of the bail application and the identity of the accused. Where the\naccused is in custody, the bail application is generally supported by the pairokar's affidavit, not by the\naccused's own affidavit.\n\nNDPS Act, 1985  -  Drafting, Pleadings, Forms & Formats\n•  Wording of the prayer. A Vakalatnama is not a pleading; it confers authority. Do not import grounds into\nit.\nModel Memorandum of Appearance\nIN THE COURT OF THE LEARNED SPECIAL JUDGE (NDPS), [DISTRICT], [CITY]\n \nSC No. __ of 20__        FIR No. __ of 20        PS ____________________\n \nSTATE                                                              .... PROSECUTION\nVERSUS\n[ACCUSED]                                                          ... ACCUSED\n \nMEMORANDUM OF APPEARANCE\n \nLearned Counsel for the accused named above respectfully submits that the undersigned Advocate has been engaged by \nthe accused and enters appearance on his behalf in the above case. The Vakalatnama duly executed by the accused is filed\nherewith. It is prayed that the appearance of the undersigned may kindly be taken on record and the accused may be \npermitted to be represented through the undersigned.\n \n____________________\nADVOCATE FOR THE ACCUSED\n \nPlace: __\nDate: __\nModel Application for Exemption from Personal Appearance\nIN THE COURT OF THE LEARNED SPECIAL JUDGE (NDPS), [DISTRICT], [CITY]\nSC No. __ of 20____________________\n \nSTATE                                                              .... PROSECUTION\nVERSUS\n[ACCUSED]                                                          ... ACCUSED\n \nAPPLICATION FOR EXEMPTION FROM PERSONAL APPEARANCE ON BEHALF OF THE ACCUSED\n \nMOST RESPECTFULLY SHOWETH:\n \n1. That the accused is on bail in the above case granted by this Hon'ble Court vide order dated _, and has been regularly \nappearing before this Hon'ble Court on every date of hearing.\n \n2. That on the last date of hearing, this Hon'ble Court was pleased to grant exemption from personal appearance to the \naccused, and the accused undertakes to appear before this Hon'ble Court as and when directed.\n \n3. That the accused is employed at [place] and resides at [distance] from this Hon'ble Court; his personal presence is not \nnecessary for today's proceedings as the matter is listed for [purpose], and the accused will be represented by his counsel.\n \n4. That no prejudice will be caused to the prosecution if the exemption prayed for is granted.\n \nPRAYER\n \nIt is, therefore, most respectfully prayed that this Hon'ble Court may kindly be pleased to exempt the personal appearance \nof the accused on the present date, in the interest of justice.\n \n____________________\nADVOCATE FOR THE ACCUSED\n \nPlace: __        Date: __"
