    "id": "tpl-ndps-report-arrest-seizure-superior-57",
    "category": "ndps",
    "categoryLabel": "NDPS",
    "statute": "Narcotic Drugs and Psychotropic Substances Act, 1985 (Section 57)",
    "title": "Statutory Report of Arrest and Seizure to Superior Officer under Section 57 NDPS Act",
    "shortDesc": "Official detailed report of arrest and seizure submitted by the empowered officer to his immediate superior officer within forty-eight hours under Section 57 NDPS.",
    "limitationNotice": "48-Hour Deadline: Must be submitted to immediate official superior within 48 hours next after arrest and seizure.",
    "tags": [
      "Section 57 NDPS",
      "Report to Superior Officer",
      "48 Hours",
      "Departmental Compliance",
      "NDPS"
    ],
    "content": "NDPS Act, 1985  -  Drafting, Pleadings, Forms & Formats\nC-10. Report of Arrest and Seizure to the Superior Officer (Section 57)\nPurpose\nThe statutory check on the field officer: a full report of all the particulars of every arrest and seizure, to be made\nto the immediate official superior within forty-eight hours.\nStatutory basis\nSection 57 of the NDPS Act, 1985; rule 5(1) of the 2022 Rules (deposit in the godown within 48 hours).\nModel report\nPOLICE STATION : ____________________     To,\nNo. __ dated __  The [Deputy Commissioner of Police / Sub-Divisional Police Officer],\n[Zone/District], [place]\n[Through the Station House Officer]\n \nREPORT UNDER SECTION 57 OF THE NDPS ACT, 1985\n \nSub : Report of arrest and seizure  -  CR/FIR No. __ of 20__, PS __, under Section(s) ____________________ of the NDPS Act, 1985.\n \nRef : This office report under section 42(2) of the Act dated __ [where applicable].\n \nSir/Madam,\n \n1. PARTICULARS OF THE CASE. FIR/CR No. __ dated __ was registered at PS __ under Section(s) __ of the NDPS \nAct, 1985, on the complaint/report of ____________________.\n \n2. PARTICULARS OF THE SEIZURE.\n(a) Date and time of seizure : __ at __ hrs;\n(b) Place of seizure : ____________________;\n(c) Description and quantity of the substance seized : ____________________;\n(d) Number of packages/containers and the serial numbers : ____________________;\n(e) Approximate value : ₹__ ;\n(f) Other articles/conveyances seized : ____________________ ;\n(g) Independent witnesses : (i) __ (ii) __ ;\n(h) Whether the search was recorded through audio-video electronic means under section 105 BNSS : Yes/No;\n(i) Whether action under sections 41/42/43 of the Act was taken in compliance with the provisions thereof, including\nthe recording of information/grounds of belief : Yes/No  -  details ____________________.\n \n3. PARTICULARS OF THE ARREST.\n(a) Name(s), parentage and address of the person(s) arrested : ____________________ ;\n(b) Date and time of arrest : __ at __ hrs ;\n(c) Grounds of arrest informed in writing : Yes/No ;\n(d) Whether the person was informed of his right under section 50 of the Act (where a personal search was involved)\n: Yes/No ;\n(e) Person informed of the arrest : ____________________ ;\n(f) Date and time of production before the Magistrate : __ at __ hrs ;\n(g) Present custody of the arrested person(s) : [judicial custody in Central Jail __ / police custody vide order dated __\n/ released on bail vide order dated __].\n \n4. CUSTODY OF THE CASE PROPERTY. The seized material has been deposited in the godown at __ on __ at __ \nhrs under Form-1 No. __ and Form-2 acknowledgment No. __ [or: the material is being produced before the Learned \nMagistrate for certification under section 52-A on ____________________].\n \n5. STAGE OF INVESTIGATION. [Briefly state the further investigation proposed  -  collection of the FSL report; \nexamination of witnesses; tracing the source; whether any other accused is to be traced.]\n \n6. REMARKS. The case property is intact and sealed; the godown entries are up to date; the sample has been despatched \nto the laboratory on __. No untoward incident occurred during the operation.\n \n\nNDPS Act, 1985  -  Drafting, Pleadings, Forms & Formats\nYours faithfully,\n____________________\n(Signature of the Investigating / Seizing Officer)\nName, rank, designation : ____________________\n \nAcknowledgment of the superior officer : ____________________  dated : __\nDrafting notes\n•  48 hours, no extension. Section 57 admits of no relaxation, and the report is the record of what was seized\nand arrested. Delay is regularly put to the IO in cross-examination.\n•  The report must be \"full\". The particulars of the arrest, the seizure, the place, the witnesses, the custody of\nthe property and the grounds of belief are all to be included; a cyclostyled form with the facts left to the case\ndiary does not satisfy the section.\n•  The report supplements sections 42(2) and 52(2)-(3). Under section 42(2) the copy of the information\ngoes to the superior forthwith; under section 57 the report of the arrest and seizure goes within 48 hours;\nunder section 52(2)-(3) the person and the articles are forwarded without unnecessary delay to the officer-\nin-charge of the police station or an officer empowered under section 53. All three should be able to stand\ntogether in the file.\n•  Defence use of the report. In cross-examination, the report is used to test the time of the seizure, the time of\nthe deposit in the godown, the identity of the witnesses and the consistency of the narrative with the FIR and\nthe panchnama."
